+# Agent Note: Re-probe the Microsoft Store pwsh executable
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-01-reprobe-store-pwsh-executable.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A Store app execution alias is a mutable indirection to a versioned package executable. Accepting every link-shaped PATH entry and caching its path for the executor lifetime lets a dangling alias reach `spawn`, and an alias or package replacement after host startup leaves the executor on stale filesystem state. The resulting `ENOENT` is reported as a missing `pwsh` tool even when a viable PowerShell 7 package executable or a repaired alias exists.
+
+## Decision
+
+Automatic Windows resolution validates each link-shaped candidate's target before selection. A readable Store alias resolves to its current package executable, target inspection denied by ACL retains the alias for CreateProcess, and a missing target falls through to the next candidate. An explicit `pwshPath` remains authoritative without probing.
+
+`PwshLocalExecutor.pwshPath` repeats automatic resolution for every spawn instead of caching it at construction. Each call therefore observes Store package updates, alias repair, and legacy fallback availability while preserving explicit configuration and sandbox argv wrapping.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Accept every link-shaped candidate and fail at spawn.** Rejected because a dangling alias can mask viable later candidates and because a repaired installation remains unusable until the long-lived executor reloads.
+
+**Always fall through to Windows PowerShell 5.1 when alias target inspection fails.** Rejected because Store package directories may intentionally deny target inspection even though CreateProcess can use the alias; that would silently select a different shell.
+
+**Probe the versioned WindowsApps package directory independently of the alias.** Rejected because the alias already owns package selection and exposes its current target without duplicating Store package naming or version policy.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A valid readable Store install launches its concrete PowerShell 7 package executable, a protected valid alias remains supported, and a confirmed dangling alias cannot shadow later candidates. Automatic resolution performs a small synchronous filesystem probe per spawn; explicit `pwshPath` avoids it. Pure tests cover readable targets, dangling targets, and repair between consecutive resolutions, while the real-process suite still verifies the selected executable through the subprocess service.
